-- Records the honest, investigated-not-assumed finding on the "Agent
-- Factory" (dynamic runtime agent composition/creation with governed
-- permissions/skills/connections) called for in the FINAL MASTER
-- CONVERGENCE brief, per its own explicit instruction not to fake agent
-- creation if the architecture cannot actually instantiate it. Applied
-- live via Supabase MCP on 2026-09-02; this file makes it reproducible
-- from a fresh database.

insert into public.capability_registry
  (capability_key, name, description, category, skill, agent_tool_name, package_or_module, department, connection, required_permission, read_write, tenant_scope, cost_profile, risk, verification_method, status, status_notes, external_blocker, last_verified_at, last_verified_by)
values
  ('capability:agent_factory_dynamic_composition', 'Agent Factory -- dynamic runtime agent composition/creation with governed permissions/skills/connections', 'The FINAL MASTER CONVERGENCE brief calls for an "Agent Factory": the ability to dynamically compose/create a new agent at runtime with its own governed permission set, skill list, and connection scope, with an explicit instruction not to fake this if the architecture cannot actually instantiate it. Investigated directly rather than assumed: packages/workforce-core''s departments/roles/capabilities registries (Update 17) -- the only real "agent-shaped" registries in this codebase -- are 100% compile-time, source-code-defined data (DEPARTMENT_REGISTRY/ROLE_REGISTRY/capabilities registry.ts, all Object.fromEntries over a literal array; DepartmentKey/CapabilityKey are TypeScript literal unions, not database-backed enums). The actual, single, canonical agent runtime (packages/agent-core''s runAgentTurn) resolves its tool set from a hardcoded array literal (lib/agent-core/copilot-actions.ts''s extraTools: [...]), assembled identically on every single request -- there is no per-row, per-tenant, or per-principal dynamic tool/skill/connection resolution anywhere in the codebase, and no persisted "agent definition" concept at all (no table, no CRUD, no create_agent tool). A real Agent Factory needs four pieces, none of which exist even as a stub: (1) a persisted agent-definition record (name, department, allowed skill/tool keys, connection scope, permission profile, created_by); (2) a dynamic tool-resolver that builds a real, permission-checked AgentTool[] subset per agent-definition row at request time, replacing today''s fixed array; (3) a creation flow enforcing that a new agent''s requested permissions are always a subset of the creating principal''s own (never privilege escalation); (4) a real dispatch surface for actually reaching a dynamically-created agent (new WhatsApp binding type, named mission type, or Admin surface). Building even a minimal, honestly-real version of this is a multi-file, multi-week-scale architecture change (new table + new dynamic resolution layer replacing the current static one + governance + dispatch), not a safe same-session increment like every other item shipped this pass -- and a stub version (e.g. a table with no real dynamic dispatch behind it) would itself be exactly the fabrication the brief explicitly warned against. Correctly left unattempted this pass per the user''s own confirmed instruction: do not fabricate completion on things that cannot be done safely in-session.', 'ecosystem', null, null, 'packages/workforce-core/src/{departments,roles,capabilities}; lib/agent-core/copilot-actions.ts; packages/agent-core/src/orchestrator.ts', 'Engineering', null, null, 'read_write', 'platform_only', 'free', 'high_risk', 'Read packages/workforce-core''s departments/roles/capabilities registry source directly (all three are Object.fromEntries over compile-time literal arrays, no DB table backing any of them) and lib/agent-core/copilot-actions.ts''s extraTools assembly (one fixed array literal, identical on every request, no per-agent/per-tenant resolution). Confirmed no create_agent, agent_definitions table, or any dynamic tool-resolution function exists anywhere in the repository.', 'NOT_BUILT', 'Requires a genuine, multi-file architecture change (persisted agent-definition record, a dynamic tool-resolver replacing the current static extraTools array, a governed creation flow, and a real dispatch surface) -- correctly not attempted as a same-session increment. A future, deliberate build of this should start with the dynamic tool-resolver (the one piece every other requirement depends on), keeping the existing static extraTools array as the default/fallback agent definition so today''s WhatsApp/Admin Copilot behavior is preserved exactly.', null, now(), 'claude_session_2026-09-02')
on conflict (capability_key) do nothing;
